.\"	$GergiOS: audit2txt.8,v 1.0 2026/07/10 $
.\"
.Dd July 10, 2026
.Dt AUDIT2TXT 8
.Os GergiOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm audit2txt
.Nd format audit log files for human reading
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Fl p Ar endpoint
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads audit log files produced by
.Xr auditd 8
and formats them as a human-readable, aligned table.
.Pp
The input format is pipe-delimited text:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
serial|timestamp_ticks|type_name|result|subject|object|extra_hex
.Ed
.Pp
The output format is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[HH:MM:SS.mmm]  TYPE           subj=X  obj=Y  result=NAME  extra
.Ed
.Pp
If no
.Ar file
is given, or if
.Ar file
is
.Sq - ,
standard input is read.
Each file is processed in sequence.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl f
Follow mode.
After reading existing content,
.Nm
waits for new records to be appended, similar to
.Xr tail 1
.Fl f .
Useful for monitoring live audit logs.
.It Fl t Ar type
Filter output to show only events of the given
.Ar type .
Valid types include:
.Cm AUTH_SUCCESS ,
.Cm AUTH_FAILURE ,
.Cm PRIV_CHANGE ,
.Cm IPC_DENIED ,
.Cm FILE_DENIED ,
.Cm DEVICE_BIND ,
.Cm SYSCALL_AUTH ,
.Cm MAC_VIOLATION ,
.Cm SERVICE_START ,
.Cm SERVICE_CRASH .
.It Fl p Ar endpoint
Filter output to show only events that involve the given process
.Ar endpoint
(either as subject or object).
.It Fl h
Show usage summary.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/log/audit/audit.log -compact
.It Pa /var/log/audit/audit.log
Default audit log file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Display the entire current audit log:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit2txt /var/log/audit/audit.log
.Ed
.Pp
Monitor live audit events:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit2txt -f /var/log/audit/audit.log
.Ed
.Pp
Show only denied file access events:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit2txt -t FILE_DENIED /var/log/audit/audit.log
.Ed
.Pp
Show all events involving process endpoint 2 (RS):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit2txt -p 2 /var/log/audit/audit.log
.Ed
.Pp
View all rotated logs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
audit2txt /var/log/audit/audit.log.*
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr auditd 8 ,
.Xr auditctl 8 ,
.Xr auditd.conf 5
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in GergiOS 1.0.
